{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1381458-i-d-like-to-ask-your-expertise","id":1381458,"title":"I'd like to ask your expertise...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-14T15:46:50-07:00","id":1381458,"title":"I'd like to ask your expertise...","content":"...In both Mage's metaphysics and polynesian myth.<br /> According to Gods and Monsters. Pele and Tane and more are part of Mage's World of Darkness. I'm curious, what about Maui? Is he also a Godgformn? Or would you think he is a Mage or even archmage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T16:48:35-07:00","id":1381470,"title":"","content":"I think it depends on the Maui you are asking about. There are numerous versions of Maui (singular) and there are many examples of different beings using the name Maui (plural). I would also disregard the concept of Polynesia when trying to understand the peoples of the Pacific. Oceania and the Indigenous Pacific are more inclusive (though also hotly debated) terms and conceptualizations of the political, social, and material relations found in this area traditionally, historically, and contemporarily. Moreover, for many peoples of this region, their cosmological and epistemological views are land-based, specific stories connected to the land should be understood as the primary point of reference instead of some presumed connection between peoples. For example, Pele is an inhabitant of Kilauea whereas T\u0101ne is the Maori sky father. So, while Indigenous Pacific gods might appear to be similar (think T\u0101ne and K\u0101ne) (and actually genealogically related) they are also distinct at the same time. <br /> <br /> This is all to say that the metaphysics of Mage are actually pretty limited in its ability to include the cosmologies that are incommensurate with its general approach of cultural relativism. This is important to take into consideration given that forms of Maui and/or references to a Maui are found as far west from Hawaii as New Guinea. Maui from Hawaii could be a God form, a mage (possibly even an archmage or ascended), an important chief who did all of the things in the stories during a time when humans were closer to the land and their other kin, a real life family member most Hawaiians can cite in their family lineage, something else entirely, or all of these things at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T17:31:22-07:00","id":1381475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1381458-i-d-like-to-ask-your-expertise?p=1381470#post1381470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it depends on the Maui you are asking about. There are numerous versions of Maui (singular) and there are many examples of different beings using the name Maui (plural). I would also disregard the concept of Polynesia when trying to understand the peoples of the Pacific. Oceania and the Indigenous Pacific are more inclusive (though also hotly debated) terms and conceptualizations of the political, social, and material relations found in this area traditionally, historically, and contemporarily. Moreover, for many peoples of this region, their cosmological and epistemological views are land-based, specific stories connected to the land should be understood as the primary point of reference instead of some presumed connection between peoples. For example, Pele is an inhabitant of Kilauea whereas T\u0101ne is the Maori sky father. So, while Indigenous Pacific gods might appear to be similar (think T\u0101ne and K\u0101ne) (and actually genealogically related) they are also distinct at the same time.<br /> <br /> This is all to say that the metaphysics of Mage are actually pretty limited in its ability to include the cosmologies that are incommensurate with its general approach of cultural relativism. This is important to take into consideration given that forms of Maui and/or references to a Maui are found as far west from Hawaii as New Guinea. Maui from Hawaii could be a God form, a mage (possibly even an archmage or ascended), an important chief who did all of the things in the stories during a time when humans were closer to the land and their other kin, a real life family member most Hawaiians can cite in their family lineage, something else entirely, or all of these things at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks Iladas!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T18:31:55-07:00","id":1381495,"title":"","content":"Look over the Book of Crafts (pages 63-78) and Dead Magic 2 (pages 12-39, the chapter called Sad Islands in the Seas) for official treatments of Polynesia in Mage prior to Gods and Monsters.<br /> <br /> Mage has pretty broad metaphysics, so I would consider two questions pretty important:<br /> <br /> 1. How do you do appropriate justice to the stories you are working with?<br /> 2. What makes the game most fun while avoiding negative stereotypes and misinformation?<br /> <br /> Mage: the Ascension is a game where you're probably not going to get it all right, because it's real world beliefs tweaked to fit a game. That being said, you can get it more right by doing homework with due care.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}